+/**
+ * Accessors for the fields `lv_draw_sw_thread_dsc_t` shares between a render
+ * thread and the thread that dispatches and frees draw tasks. Every access to
+ * `task_act` and `exit_status` must go through these.
+ *
+ * Neither is synchronised on the field itself. `task_act` is the one that
+ * matters most: `wait_for_finish()` checks it to decide when no draw unit is
+ * still blending into a layer buffer, and `lv_draw_cleanup_task()` destroys
+ * that buffer as soon as the check passes. When the render thread has already
+ * cleared it, the check returns without touching `task_done_sync`, so a plain
+ * read establishes no happens-before edge with the render thread's pixel
+ * writes. Carrying the ordering on the field is what makes the guard mean what
+ * it says, and is the only form ThreadSanitizer can model.
